                                "example_id": "8045b905-3b12-45b0-864f-7832c83f3650",
                                "sense_id": "d7500d20-b759-31ac-844e-b1162c7121f8",
                                "text": "At the end of August Eaton anchored at a group of three small islands off the coast of Fujian to take on fresh water, as the casks had not been refilled since leaving the Cape in April. Cuninghame calls these islands the Crocodile Islands, but he says the Chinese call them the ‘Pek-kin Islands’. These are the Matsu Islands, north east of Fuzhou, one of which is called Peikantang or Peikan Island."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "fbea5d5f-d6fc-469a-8574-b2161cbf06b2",
                                "sense_id": "d7500d20-b759-31ac-844e-b1162c7121f8",
                                "text": "In a past life in Fuzhou, it represented some reality other than the one of daily congee and pickled turnips, cabbage and boiled rip soup."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
